**Step 1:** Expanding the sum, we have
\begin{equation}
\sum_{k = 1}^{1728} \frac{1}{1 + \omega^k + \omega^{2k} + \omega^{3k}} = \sum_{k = 1}^{1728}\left( \frac{1}{1 - \omega^{3k}} - \frac{1}{1 - \omega^k} + \frac{1}{1 - \omega^{4k}} \right)
\end{equation}

**Step 2:** Now we can rewrite the sum using the formula for the sum of a geometric series:
\begin{equation}
\sum_{k = 0}^{1728}\frac{1}{1 - \omega^{3k}} = \frac{1}{1 - \omega^3}\cdot\frac{1}{1 - \omega^{3\cdot1728}} = \frac{1}{1 - \omega^3} \cdot \frac{1}{\omega^{5824} - 1},
\end{equation}

\begin{equation}
\sum_{k = 0}^{1728}\frac{1}{1 - \omega^k} = \frac{1}{1 - \omega}\cdot\frac{1}{1 - \omega^{1728}} = \frac{1}{1 - \omega} \cdot \frac{1}{\omega^{1729} - 1},
\end{equation}

\begin{equation}
\sum_{k = 0}^{1728}\frac{1}{1 - \omega^{4k}} = \frac{1}{1 - \omega^4}\cdot\frac{1}{1 - \omega^{4\cdot1728}} = \frac{1}{1 - \omega^4} \cdot \frac{1}{\omega^{6896} - 1}.
\end{equation}

As a result,
\begin{align}
\sum_{k = 1}^{1728} \frac{1}{1 + \omega^k + \omega^{2k} + \omega^{3k}} &= \frac{1}{1 - \omega^3} \cdot \frac{1}{\omega^{5824} - 1} - \frac{1}{1 - \omega} \cdot \frac{1}{\omega^{1729} - 1} + \frac{1}{1 - \omega^4} \cdot \frac{1}{\omega^{6896} - 1}\\
&= \frac{1}{\omega^{5824} - \omega^3}\cdot \frac{1}{1 - \omega^3} - \frac{1}{\omega^{1729} - \omega}\cdot \frac{1}{1 - \omega} + \frac{1}{\omega^{6896} - \omega^4}\cdot \frac{1}{1 - \omega^4}\\
\boxed{\text{final answer is} & \ \ \ \ \frac{1}{\omega^{5824} - \omega^3} - \frac{\omega^{1729}}{\omega^{1729} - \omega} + \frac{\omega^{6896}}{\omega^{6896} - \omega^4}}
\end{align}
