* Calculate the area of the first triangle (Triangle 1) by the formula $ Area = \frac{1}{2}base \times height $. Calculate the area of the second triangle (Triangle 2) by subtracting the area of the first triangle from the area of the quadrilateral made by closing off the third and fourth triangles.

* The area of the pentagon is equal to the sum of the areas of the two triangles.

