Using this, the surface area (in square meters) can be calculated as:

\boxed{6 * ( \sqrt[3]{0.027} )^2 = 6 * (0.08610637 \approx 0.086106) ^ 2 = \boxed{6 * (0.0071432 \approx 0.0071432) } (\text{square meters})}

