\boxed{\text{ The surface area is }}

The length of one side, , of a cube is its volume raised to the power of one third:
$$ a = \sqrt[3]{0.027 \text{ cubic meters}} $$

The total surface area of a cube can be calculated by multiplying by six the square of the length of one side:
$$ 6 a^2 = 6 \left( \sqrt[3]{0.027 \text{ cubic meters}} \right)^2 $$

Let's calculate the surface area of the given cube:
\begin{align*}
6 a^2 &= 6 \left( \sqrt[3]{0.027 \text{ cubic meters}} \right)^2 \\
&= 6 \times \left( \left( \sqrt[3]{0.027 \text{ cubic meters}} \right)^2 \times 1 \right) \\
&= 6 \times \left( \left( 0.027 \text{ cubic meters} \right)^\frac{2}{3} \right)^2 \\
&= 6 \times \left( \left( \sqrt[3]{(0.027)^2} \right)^2 \right) \\
&= 6 \times \left( 0.027 \text{ cubic meters}^{2/3} \right)^2 \\
&= 6 \times 0.027^2 \text{ cubic meters}^{2} \\
&= 0.309 \text{ square cubic meters}
\end{align*}

Since there is a conversion factor for cubic meters to square meters (1 cubic meter is equal to 1,000,000 square meters):
\begin{align*}
\text{The surface area is } &= 0.309 \text{ square cubic meters} \\
&= 0.309 \times 1,000,000 \text{ square meters} \\
&= \boxed{309,000 \text{ square meters}}
\end{align*}

